+//! Where the ordering requirement goes: one key per group, and nothing to order, no group.
+//!
+//! There is no global order across a topic's partitions. What a course can teach instead is the
+//! design move this step is about: take the pairs of events that must stay ordered and make them
+//! share a key — the connected groups of the "must be ordered" graph. Everything else stays free to
+//! be parallel, because a key nobody needs to share is a partition nobody needs to serialize.
+//!
+//! ## What you write
+//!
+//! [`plan`] — a key per event, such that two events named in one ordering rule share a key, and
+//! events no rule connects do not. A group's key is the smallest event name in it, which is a
+//! deterministic choice; a rule naming an event outside `events` is ignored.
+
